/-!
# Irreducible generators of finite-state tree automorphisms

For every finite alphabet of at least two letters, the group of finite-state automorphisms of
the rooted tree of words admits a generating set minimal under inclusion.
This is Lavrenyuk's Theorem 3.8 in *Minimal generating sets in wreath products*.

The proof uses the permutation of the first level and the sections at its vertices. Write
`H` for the finite-state group and `V` for its quotient by the subgroup generated by squares.
In two child subtrees choose pairs `(a, b)` whose images in `V` under multiplication are
linearly independent over the field of two elements. Enumerate the countable group `H`. For each
`b` in that enumeration, choose an involution `a` so the new pair avoids the finite span of
its predecessors. Flips at different depths supply infinitely many distinct square classes for
this choice. Extend the family until it spans `V`.

Squaring the chosen pairs yields every square in a single coordinate. Exchanging the two
coordinates then gives diagonal elements and finally the entire two-coordinate group.
A minimal generating set for the root permutations moves these actions to every child.
The root action detects omission of a root generator, and the sum of the section classes in `V`
detects omission of a pair.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FiniteStateIrreducibleGeneratorsKourovka16Problem86Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.86 (V. I.
Sushchanskiĭ). UnsolvedMath record UM-00701277 (`KOU-16.86`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

The `d`-regular rooted tree (`d ≥ 2`) has the words `List (Fin d)` as vertices. A tree automorphism
is a permutation `g` of the words with `g (v ++ w) = g v ++ u` for a word `u` of the length of `w`;
its section at `v` is the map `w ↦ u`, and `g` is finite-state when it has finitely many distinct
sections. The group is the subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (List (Fin d))` generated by the finite-state
automorphisms, which consists of exactly them. An irreducible system of generators is a generating
set no proper subset of which generates (a minimal generating set, Lavrenyuk's term). The target is
stated for every `d ≥ 2`: Lavrenyuk's regular rooted tree is the tree of words over any finite
alphabet of at least two letters (arXiv:1210.0150, Section 3).
-/

/-- **Kourovka Problem 16.86 (Sushchanskiĭ): irreducible generators of finite-state automorphism
groups.** The statement that for every integer $d \ge 2$ the group of finite-state automorphisms of
the $d$-regular rooted tree has an irreducible system of generators: a set $S$ of elements of the
group that generates the group and no proper subset of which generates the group. -/
def finiteStateAutomorphismsIrreducibleGenerators : Prop :=
  ∀ d : ℕ, 2 ≤ d → ∃ S : Set (finiteStateAutomorphisms d),
    Subgroup.closure S = ⊤ ∧
      ∀ T : Set (finiteStateAutomorphisms d), T ⊂ S → Subgroup.closure T ≠ ⊤

variable {d : ℕ}

private abbrev Word (d : ℕ) := List (Fin d)

private theorem sec_append {g : Equiv.Perm (Word d)} (hg : IsTreeAutomorphism g) (v u w) :
    treeSection g v (u ++ w) = treeSection g v u ++ treeSection g (v ++ u) w := by
  apply List.append_cancel_left (as := g v)
  calc
    _ = g ((v ++ u) ++ w) := by rw [List.append_assoc, ← hg.map_append_section]
    _ = _ := by rw [hg.map_append_section (v ++ u), hg.map_append_section v u, List.append_assoc]

private abbrev Machine (d : ℕ) :=
  (n : ℕ) × Fin n × (Fin n → Fin d → Word d) × (Fin n → Fin d → Fin n)

private def run {n : ℕ} (out : Fin n → Fin d → Word d) (step : Fin n → Fin d → Fin n)
    (q : Fin n) : Word d → Word d
  | [] => []
  | x :: xs => out q x ++ run out step (step q x) xs

private theorem runs_machine {g : Equiv.Perm (Word d)}
    (hg : IsTreeAutomorphism g ∧ (Set.range (treeSection g)).Finite) :
    ∃ M : Machine d, ∀ w, g w = run M.2.2.1 M.2.2.2 M.2.1 w := by
  classical
  let Q := Set.range (treeSection g)
  have : Finite Q := hg.2
  obtain ⟨n, ⟨e⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin Q
  let v (q : Fin n) := (e.symm q).property.choose
  let state (u : Word d) : Fin n := e ⟨treeSection g u, u, rfl⟩
  let step (q : Fin n) (a : Fin d) := state (v q ++ [a])
  let out (q : Fin n) (a : Fin d) := treeSection g (v q) [a]
  have hv (q) : treeSection g (v q) = (e.symm q).val := (e.symm q).property.choose_spec
  have hs (u) : (e.symm (state u)).val = treeSection g u := by simp [state]
  have h (w : Word d) (q) : (e.symm q).val w = run out step q w := by
    induction w generalizing q with
    | nil => simp [← hv, treeSection, run]
    | cons a xs ih =>
      change _ = out q a ++ run out step (step q a) xs
      rw [← hv, ← List.singleton_append, sec_append hg.1, ← ih]
      rw [hs]
  refine ⟨⟨n, state [], out, step⟩, fun w => ?_⟩
  simpa [hs, treeSection, hg.1.map_nil] using h w (state [])

private theorem finiteState_countable : Countable (finiteStateAutomorphisms d) := by
  classical
  let enc (g : finiteStateAutomorphisms d) :=
    (runs_machine ((mem_finiteStateAutomorphisms_iff_finite_sections _).mp g.property)).choose
  have spec (g : finiteStateAutomorphisms d) :=
    (runs_machine ((mem_finiteStateAutomorphisms_iff_finite_sections _).mp g.property)).choose_spec
  have inj : Function.Injective enc := by
    intro g h eqn
    apply Subtype.ext
    apply Equiv.ext
    intro w
    rw [spec g w, spec h w]
    change run (enc g).2.2.1 (enc g).2.2.2 (enc g).2.1 w = _
    rw [eqn]
  exact inj.countable

private abbrev G (d : ℕ) := finiteStateAutomorphisms d

private theorem good (g : G d) :
    IsTreeAutomorphism g.val ∧ (Set.range (treeSection g.val)).Finite :=
  (mem_finiteStateAutomorphisms_iff_finite_sections _).mp g.property

private noncomputable def letter (g : G d) (a : Fin d) : Fin d :=
  (List.length_eq_one_iff.mp ((good g).1.length_apply [a])).choose

private theorem letter_spec (g : G d) (a : Fin d) : g.val [a] = [letter g a] :=
  (List.length_eq_one_iff.mp ((good g).1.length_apply [a])).choose_spec

private noncomputable def rootPerm (g : G d) : Equiv.Perm (Fin d) where
  toFun := letter g
  invFun := letter g⁻¹
  left_inv a := by
    have e : g.val.symm (g.val [a]) = [a] := g.val.symm_apply_apply _
    rw [letter_spec g] at e
    change (g⁻¹ : G d).val [letter g a] = [a] at e
    rwa [letter_spec, List.singleton_inj] at e
  right_inv a := by
    have e : g.val ((g⁻¹ : G d).val [a]) = [a] := g.val.apply_symm_apply _
    rwa [letter_spec g⁻¹, letter_spec g, List.singleton_inj] at e

private noncomputable def rootHom : G d →* Equiv.Perm (Fin d) where
  toFun := rootPerm
  map_one' := by
    apply Equiv.ext
    intro a
    exact List.singleton_inj.mp (letter_spec 1 a).symm
  map_mul' g h := by
    apply Equiv.ext
    intro a
    have e : (g * h).val [a] = g.val (h.val [a]) := rfl
    rwa [letter_spec (g * h), letter_spec h, letter_spec g, List.singleton_inj] at e

private noncomputable def stateAt (g : G d) (v : Word d) : G d := by
  let s := Equiv.ofBijective (treeSection g.val v) ((good g).1.bijective_treeSection v)
  refine ⟨s, (mem_finiteStateAutomorphisms_iff_finite_sections _).2 ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · intro x y
    obtain ⟨z, hl, hz⟩ := (good g).1 (v ++ x) y
    refine ⟨z, hl, ?_⟩
    change treeSection g.val v (x ++ y) = _ ++ z
    rw [sec_append (good g).1]
    congr 1
    simp [treeSection, -List.append_assoc, hz]
  · apply (good g).2.subset
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨v ++ x, ?_⟩
    funext y
    change treeSection g.val (v ++ x) y =
      (treeSection g.val v (x ++ y)).drop (treeSection g.val v x).length
    rw [sec_append (good g).1, List.drop_left]

private theorem act_cons (g : G d) (a : Fin d) (w : Word d) :
    g.val (a :: w) = rootHom g a :: (stateAt g [a]).val w := by
  change g.val (a :: w) = letter g a :: treeSection g.val [a] w
  simpa only [letter_spec g, List.singleton_append] using (good g).1.map_append_section [a] w

private theorem state_mul (g h : G d) (a : Fin d) :
    stateAt (g * h) [a] = stateAt g [rootHom h a] * stateAt h [a] := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply Equiv.ext
  intro w
  have e : (g * h).val (a :: w) = g.val (h.val (a :: w)) := rfl
  exact (List.cons.inj (by rwa [act_cons (g * h), act_cons h, act_cons g] at e : _)).2

private noncomputable def stateProd {A : Type*} [CommGroup A] (p : G d →* A) : G d →* A := by
  let f (g : G d) := ∏ a : Fin d, p (stateAt g [a])
  apply MonoidHom.mk' f
  intro g h
  simp only [f, state_mul, map_mul, Finset.prod_mul_distrib]
  congr 1
  exact Equiv.prod_comp (rootHom h) (fun a => p (stateAt g [a]))

private def assemblePerm (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) (s : Fin d → G d) : Equiv.Perm (Word d) where
  toFun
    | [] => []
    | a :: w => r a :: (s a).val w
  invFun
    | [] => []
    | a :: w => r.symm a :: (s (r.symm a)).val.symm w
  left_inv := by rintro (_ | ⟨a, w⟩) <;> simp
  right_inv := by rintro (_ | ⟨a, w⟩) <;> simp

private def assemble (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) (s : Fin d → G d) : G d := by
  let f := assemblePerm r s
  apply Subtype.mk f
  apply (mem_finiteStateAutomorphisms_iff_finite_sections _).2
  constructor
  · rintro (_ | ⟨a, v⟩) w
    · refine ⟨f w, ?_, rfl⟩
      cases w with
      | nil => rfl
      | cons a w => simp [f, assemblePerm, (good (s a)).1.length_apply]
    · obtain ⟨u, hu, he⟩ := (good (s a)).1 v w
      exact ⟨u, hu, congrArg (List.cons (r a)) he⟩
  · have h := (Set.finite_singleton (treeSection f [])).union
        (Set.finite_iUnion (fun a : Fin d => (good (s a)).2))
    apply h.subset
    rintro _ ⟨_ | ⟨a, v⟩, rfl⟩
    · exact Or.inl rfl
    · exact Or.inr (Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨a, v, rfl⟩)

private theorem gext {g h : G d}
    (eqn : ∀ a w, g.val (a :: w) = h.val (a :: w)) : g = h := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply Equiv.ext
  rintro (_ | ⟨a, w⟩)
  · rw [(good g).1.map_nil, (good h).1.map_nil]
  · exact eqn a w

private noncomputable def rootLift : Equiv.Perm (Fin d) →* G d :=
  MonoidHom.mk' (fun r => assemble r (fun _ => 1)) fun _ _ => gext fun _ _ => rfl

private noncomputable def baseLift : (Fin d → G d) →* G d :=
  MonoidHom.mk' (fun s => assemble 1 s) fun _ _ => gext fun _ _ => rfl

private noncomputable def localAt (a : Fin d) : G d →* G d :=
  baseLift.comp (MonoidHom.mulSingle (fun _ : Fin d => G d) a)

private theorem root_local (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) (a : Fin d) (g : G d) :
    rootLift r * localAt a g * (rootLift r)⁻¹ = localAt (r a) g := by
  rw [← map_inv]
  apply gext
  intro b w
  change r (r.symm b) :: (Pi.mulSingle (M := fun _ : Fin d => G d) a g (r.symm b)).val w =
    b :: (Pi.mulSingle (M := fun _ : Fin d => G d) (r a) g b).val w
  by_cases e : b = r a
  · subst b
    simp
  · have hn : r.symm b ≠ a := by simpa [Equiv.symm_apply_eq] using e
    simp [Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne e, Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne hn]

private theorem state_assemble (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) (s : Fin d → G d) (a : Fin d) :
    stateAt (assemble r s) [a] = s a := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  apply Equiv.ext
  intro w
  change (r a :: (s a).val w).drop (r a :: (s a).val []).length = _
  simp [(good (s a)).1.map_nil]

private theorem root_assemble (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) (s : Fin d → G d) :
    rootHom (assemble r s) = r := by
  apply Equiv.ext
  intro a
  have e := letter_spec (assemble r s) a
  change r a :: (s a).val [] = [letter _ a] at e
  exact (List.cons.inj e).1.symm

private theorem root_base_generate (N : Subgroup (G d))
    (hr : ∀ r, rootLift r ∈ N) (hb : ∀ a g, localAt a g ∈ N) : N = ⊤ := by
  apply top_unique
  intro g _
  have allbase (s : Fin d → G d) : baseLift s ∈ N := by
    exact Subgroup.pi_mem_of_mulSingle_mem (H := N.comap baseLift) s (fun a => hb a (s a))
  have e : g = rootLift (rootHom g) * baseLift (fun a => stateAt g [a]) := gext (act_cons g)
  exact e ▸ N.mul_mem (hr _) (allbase _)

variable {H : Type*} [Group H]

-- Swapping (a, b) gives (b, a). Their quotient has coordinates c and its inverse.
-- A square in the second coordinate then gives the diagonal (c, c).
private theorem pairs_eq_top (K : Subgroup (H × H))
    (flip : ∀ a b, (a, b) ∈ K → (b, a) ∈ K)
    (square : ∀ a : H, (a * a, 1) ∈ K)
    (gen : Subgroup.closure ({h | ∃ a b, (a, b) ∈ K ∧ h = a * b⁻¹} ∪
      Set.range (fun h : H => h * h)) = ⊤) : K = ⊤ := by
  let U : Set H := {h | ∃ a b, (a, b) ∈ K ∧ h = a * b⁻¹} ∪ Set.range (fun h => h * h)
  change Subgroup.closure U = ⊤ at gen
  have diag (h : H) : (h, h) ∈ K := by
    have le : Subgroup.closure U ≤ K.comap ((MonoidHom.id H).prod (MonoidHom.id H)) := by
      apply (Subgroup.closure_le _).2
      rintro x (⟨a, b, hab, rfl⟩ | ⟨a, rfl⟩)
      · have e := K.mul_mem (K.mul_mem hab (K.inv_mem (flip _ _ hab)))
                    (flip _ _ (square (a * b⁻¹)))
        change (a * b⁻¹, a * b⁻¹) ∈ K
        simpa [mul_assoc] using e
      · exact (by simpa using K.mul_mem (square a) (flip _ _ (square a)) :
          (a * a, a * a) ∈ K)
    exact le (gen.ge (Subgroup.mem_top h))
  have pure (h : H) : (h, 1) ∈ K := by
    have le : Subgroup.closure U ≤ K.comap (MonoidHom.inl H H) := by
      apply (Subgroup.closure_le _).2
      rintro x (⟨a, b, hab, rfl⟩ | ⟨a, rfl⟩)
      · exact (by simpa using K.mul_mem hab (diag b⁻¹) : (a * b⁻¹, 1) ∈ K)
      · exact square a
    exact le (gen.ge (Subgroup.mem_top h))
  apply top_unique
  rintro ⟨a, b⟩ _
  simpa using K.mul_mem (pure a) (flip _ _ (pure b))

-- At stage n, reserve a pair for the nth group element before extending to a basis.
private theorem choose_pairs {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module (ZMod 2) V] [Countable H]
    (v : H × H → V) (hv : ∀ b : H, (v '' {x | x.2 = b ∧ x.1 * x.1 = 1}).Infinite) :
    ∃ S : Set (H × H), LinearIndepOn (ZMod 2) v S ∧
      (∀ x, v x ∈ Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (v '' S)) ∧
      ∀ b : H, ∃ a : H, a * a = 1 ∧ (a, b) ∈ S := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨enum, he⟩ := exists_surjective_nat H
  have fresh (s : Finset (H × H)) (b : H) : ∃ x : H × H,
      (x.2 = b ∧ x.1 * x.1 = 1) ∧ v x ∉ Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (v '' (s : Set (H × H))) := by
    let W := Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (v '' (s : Set (H × H)))
    have : Module.Finite (ZMod 2) W := Module.Finite.span_of_finite _ (s.finite_toSet.image v)
    have : Finite W := Module.finite_of_finite (ZMod 2)
    obtain ⟨_, ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩, ho⟩ := (hv b).exists_notMem_finite (Set.toFinite (W : Set V))
    exact ⟨x, hx, ho⟩
  choose pick hp using fresh
  let stage : ℕ → Finset (H × H) := Nat.rec ∅ fun n s => insert (pick s (enum n)) s
  let levels (n : ℕ) : Set (H × H) := {x | x ∈ stage n}
  have mono : Monotone levels := monotone_nat_of_le_succ fun n => by
    exact Finset.subset_insert _ _
  have ind (n : ℕ) : LinearIndepOn (ZMod 2) v (levels n) := by
    induction n with
    | zero => simp [levels, stage]
    | succ n ih =>
      change LinearIndepOn (ZMod 2) v
        ((insert (pick (stage n) (enum n)) (stage n) : Finset _) : Set _)
      rw [Finset.coe_insert]
      apply LinearIndepOn.insert (K := ZMod 2) (v := v) (s := levels n) ih
      exact (hp (stage n) (enum n)).2
  have core := linearIndepOn_iUnion_of_directed mono.directed_le ind
  obtain ⟨S, _, hS, hspan, hli⟩ := exists_linearIndepOn_extension core (Set.subset_univ _)
  refine ⟨S, hli, fun x => hspan ⟨x, Set.mem_univ _, rfl⟩, fun b => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := he b
  let x := pick (stage n) (enum n)
  obtain ⟨hb, ha⟩ := (hp (stage n) (enum n)).1
  refine ⟨x.1, ha, hS (Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨n + 1, ?_⟩)⟩
  rw [← hb]
  exact Finset.mem_insert_self _ _

private def squares (H : Type*) [Group H] : Subgroup H :=
  Subgroup.closure (Set.range (fun h : H => h * h))

private instance squaresNormal : (squares H).Normal := by
  apply Subgroup.normalizer_eq_top_iff.mp
  apply top_unique
  apply Subgroup.le_normalizer_closure_iff.mpr
  rintro h _ _ ⟨g, rfl⟩
  apply Subgroup.subset_closure
  exact ⟨h * g * h⁻¹, by simp [mul_assoc]⟩

private abbrev Q (H : Type*) [Group H] := H ⧸ squares H
private abbrev qHom : H →* Q H := QuotientGroup.mk' _

private theorem qsq (a : Q H) : a * a = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨h, rfl⟩ := QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective (squares H) a
  rw [← map_mul]
  exact (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).2 (Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨h, rfl⟩)

private theorem qinv (a : Q H) : a⁻¹ = a := inv_eq_iff_mul_eq_one.mpr (qsq a)

private instance qComm : CommGroup (Q H) where
  mul_comm a b := by simpa only [mul_inv_rev, qinv] using (qinv (a * b)).symm

private instance qModule : Module (ZMod 2) (Additive (Q H)) :=
  AddCommGroup.zmodModule fun x => by
    rw [two_nsmul]
    exact qsq x.toMul

private def pairClass (x : H × H) := Additive.ofMul (qHom (x.1 * x.2⁻¹))

private theorem generate_pairs (S : Set (H × H)) (hspan : ∀ x : H × H,
    pairClass x ∈ Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (pairClass '' S))
    (hcover : ∀ b : H, ∃ a : H, a * a = 1 ∧ (a, b) ∈ S)
    (K : Subgroup (H × H)) (hS : S ⊆ K) (flip : ∀ a b, (a, b) ∈ K → (b, a) ∈ K) :
    K = ⊤ := by
  apply pairs_eq_top K flip
  · intro b
    obtain ⟨a, ha, hab⟩ := hcover b
    have h := K.mul_mem (hS hab) (hS hab)
    apply flip
    simpa [Prod.mk_mul_mk, ha] using h
  · let U : Set H := {h | ∃ a b, (a, b) ∈ K ∧ h = a * b⁻¹} ∪ Set.range (fun h => h * h)
    let L := Subgroup.closure U
    let W := AddSubgroup.toZModSubmodule 2 ((L.map qHom).toAddSubgroup)
    have incl : Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (pairClass '' S) ≤ W := by
      apply Submodule.span_le.mpr
      rintro _ ⟨⟨a, b⟩, hab, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨a * b⁻¹, Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨a, b, hS hab, rfl⟩), rfl⟩
    have hker : qHom.ker ≤ L := by
      rw [qHom, QuotientGroup.ker_mk']
      exact Subgroup.closure_mono Set.subset_union_right
    apply top_unique
    intro h _
    have hm := incl (hspan (h, 1))
    change qHom (h * (1 : H)⁻¹) ∈ L.map qHom at hm
    simp only [inv_one, mul_one] at hm
    exact (Subgroup.comap_map_eq_self hker).le hm

private theorem root_local_eq (a : Fin d) (g : G d) : rootHom (localAt a g) = 1 :=
  root_assemble _ _

private theorem prod_root {A : Type*} [CommGroup A] (p : G d →* A) (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) :
    stateProd p (rootLift r) = 1 := by
  change (∏ a, p (stateAt (assemble r (fun _ => 1)) [a])) = _
  simp [state_assemble]

private theorem prod_local {A : Type*} [CommGroup A] (p : G d →* A) (a : Fin d) (g : G d) :
    stateProd p (localAt a g) = p g := by
  change (∏ b, p (stateAt (assemble 1 (Pi.mulSingle (M := fun _ : Fin d => G d) a g)) [b])) = _
  simp only [state_assemble]
  rw [Finset.prod_eq_single a]
  · simp
  · intro b _ h
    simp [Pi.mulSingle_eq_of_ne h]
  · simp

private noncomputable def levelSign : ℕ → G d →* ℤˣ :=
  Nat.rec (Equiv.Perm.sign.comp rootHom) fun _ => stateProd

private noncomputable def flipAt (i j : Fin d) : ℕ → G d :=
  Nat.rec (rootLift (Equiv.swap i j)) fun _ => localAt i

private theorem flip_sq (i j : Fin d) (n : ℕ) : flipAt i j n * flipAt i j n = 1 := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp [flipAt, ← map_mul]
  | succ n ih =>
    change localAt i (flipAt i j n) * localAt i (flipAt i j n) = _
    rw [← map_mul, ih, map_one]

-- Only the level containing the flip has odd total sign.
private theorem flip_sign {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j) (n m : ℕ) :
    levelSign n (flipAt i j m) = if n = m then -1 else 1 := by
  induction n generalizing m with
  | zero =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      change Equiv.Perm.sign (rootHom (rootLift (Equiv.swap i j))) = _
      rw [show rootHom (rootLift (Equiv.swap i j)) = _ from root_assemble _ _]
      simp [Equiv.Perm.sign_swap hij]
    | succ m =>
      change Equiv.Perm.sign (rootHom (localAt i _)) = _
      simp [root_local_eq]
  | succ n ih =>
    cases m with
    | zero =>
      change stateProd (levelSign n) (rootLift (Equiv.swap i j)) = _
      rw [prod_root]
      simp
    | succ m => simpa [levelSign, flipAt, prod_local] using ih m

private theorem many_classes {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j) (b : G d) :
    (pairClass '' {x : G d × G d | x.2 = b ∧ x.1 * x.1 = 1}).Infinite := by
  let f (n : ℕ) := pairClass (flipAt i j n, b)
  have inj : Function.Injective f := by
    intro n m eqn
    by_contra hn
    change qHom (flipAt i j n * b⁻¹) = qHom (flipAt i j m * b⁻¹) at eqn
    simp only [map_mul, mul_left_inj] at eqn
    have hker : squares (↥(G d)) ≤ (levelSign n).ker := by
      apply (Subgroup.closure_le _).2
      rintro _ ⟨g, rfl⟩
      exact (map_mul _ _ _).trans (Int.units_mul_self _)
    have e := congrArg (QuotientGroup.lift _ (levelSign n) hker) eqn
    change levelSign n (flipAt i j n) = levelSign n (flipAt i j m) at e
    simp [flip_sign hij, hn] at e
  apply (Set.infinite_range_of_injective inj).mono
  rintro _ ⟨n, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨_, ⟨rfl, flip_sq i j n⟩, rfl⟩

private theorem loc_comm {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j) (g h : G d) :
    Commute (localAt i g) (localAt j h) :=
  (Pi.mulSingle_commute (f := fun _ : Fin d => G d) hij g h).map baseLift

private noncomputable def pairLift {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j) : G d × G d →* G d :=
  (localAt i).noncommCoprod (localAt j) (loc_comm hij)

private theorem conj_pair {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j) (a b : G d) :
    rootLift (Equiv.swap i j) * pairLift hij (a, b) * (rootLift (Equiv.swap i j))⁻¹ =
      pairLift hij (b, a) := by
  let r := rootLift (Equiv.swap i j)
  change r * (localAt i a * localAt j b) * r⁻¹ = localAt i b * localAt j a
  calc
    _ = (r * localAt i a * r⁻¹) * (r * localAt j b * r⁻¹) := by simp [mul_assoc]
    _ = _ := by simp [r, root_local, (loc_comm hij b a).eq]

private theorem pair_image {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j) (s : G d × G d) :
    stateProd qHom (pairLift hij s) = (pairClass s).toMul := by
  change stateProd qHom (localAt i s.1 * localAt j s.2) = qHom (s.1 * s.2⁻¹)
  rw [map_mul, prod_local, prod_local, map_mul, map_inv, qinv]

private theorem pair_root {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j) (s : G d × G d) :
    rootHom (pairLift hij s) = 1 := by
  change rootHom (localAt i s.1 * localAt j s.2) = 1
  simp [root_local_eq]

private theorem generating {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j)
    {R : Set (Equiv.Perm (Fin d))} (hR : Subgroup.closure R = ⊤) {S : Set (G d × G d)}
    (hs : ∀ x : G d × G d, pairClass x ∈ Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (pairClass '' S))
    (hc : ∀ b : G d, ∃ a : G d, a * a = 1 ∧ (a, b) ∈ S) :
    Subgroup.closure (rootLift '' R ∪ pairLift hij '' S) = ⊤ := by
  let N := Subgroup.closure (rootLift '' R ∪ pairLift hij '' S)
  have roots (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) : rootLift r ∈ N := by
    have h : Subgroup.closure R ≤ N.comap rootLift := (Subgroup.closure_le _).2
      (fun x hx => Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩))
    exact h (hR.ge (Subgroup.mem_top _))
  have conjmem {g : G d} (h : g ∈ N) (r : Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) :
      rootLift r * g * (rootLift r)⁻¹ ∈ N :=
    N.mul_mem (N.mul_mem (roots r) h) (N.inv_mem (roots r))
  let K := N.comap (pairLift hij)
  have hk : K = ⊤ := by
    apply generate_pairs S hs hc K
    · exact fun s h => Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨s, h, rfl⟩)
    · intro a b hab
      change pairLift hij (b, a) ∈ N
      rw [← conj_pair hij]
      exact conjmem hab _
  apply root_base_generate N roots
  intro a g
  have mempair := hk.ge (Subgroup.mem_top (g, 1))
  change localAt i g * localAt j 1 ∈ N at mempair
  rw [map_one, mul_one] at mempair
  simpa [root_local] using conjmem mempair (Equiv.swap i a)

private theorem irreducible {i j : Fin d} (hij : i ≠ j)
    {R : Set (Equiv.Perm (Fin d))} (hR : Minimal (fun A => Subgroup.closure A = ⊤) R)
    {S : Set (G d × G d)} (hli : LinearIndepOn (ZMod 2) pairClass S)
    (T : Set (G d)) (ht : T ⊂ rootLift '' R ∪ pairLift hij '' S) : Subgroup.closure T ≠ ⊤ := by
  intro hgen
  have allmem (N : Subgroup (G d)) (h : T ⊆ N) (g : G d) : g ∈ N :=
    ((Subgroup.closure_le N).2 h) (hgen.ge (Subgroup.mem_top g))
  apply ht.2
  rintro _ (⟨r, hr, rfl⟩ | ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩)
  · let A := {p ∈ R | rootLift p ∈ T}
    have h : Subgroup.closure A = ⊤ := by
      apply top_unique
      intro p _
      have h := allmem ((Subgroup.closure A).comap rootHom) (fun x hx => by
        obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ | ⟨y, _, rfl⟩ := ht.1 hx
        · change rootHom (assemble y (fun _ => 1)) ∈ Subgroup.closure A
          rw [root_assemble]
          exact Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨hy, hx⟩
        · change rootHom (pairLift hij y) ∈ Subgroup.closure A
          rw [pair_root]
          exact Subgroup.one_mem _) (rootLift p)
      change rootHom (assemble p (fun _ => 1)) ∈ Subgroup.closure A at h
      rwa [root_assemble] at h
    exact (hR.le_of_le h (fun _ hx => hx.1) hr).2
  · by_contra hn
    let W := Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (pairClass '' (S \ {s}))
    let P := W.toAddSubgroup.toSubgroup
    have h := allmem (P.comap (stateProd qHom)) (fun x hx => by
      obtain ⟨r, _, rfl⟩ | ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := ht.1 hx
      · change stateProd qHom (rootLift r) ∈ P
        rw [prod_root]
        exact P.one_mem
      · change stateProd qHom (pairLift hij y) ∈ P
        rw [pair_image]
        change pairClass y ∈ W
        apply Submodule.subset_span
        exact ⟨y, ⟨hy, fun he => hn (he ▸ hx)⟩, rfl⟩) (pairLift hij s)
    change stateProd qHom (pairLift hij s) ∈ P at h
    rw [pair_image] at h
    exact (linearIndepOn_iff_notMem_span.mp hli s hs) h

/--
**Lavrenyuk's theorem on irreducible generators of finite-state automorphism groups.** For every
integer $d \ge 2$, the group of finite-state automorphisms of the $d$-regular rooted tree has an
irreducible system of generators: a set $S$ of elements of the group that generates the group and
no proper subset of which generates the group.

Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov
(eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49
(2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 16.86 (V. I. Sushchanskiĭ); resolution: Ya. Lavrenyuk,
The group of all finite-state automorphisms of a regular rooted tree has a minimal generating set,
Geom. Dedicata 183 (2016), 59-67 (preprint: Minimal generating sets in wreath products,
arXiv:1210.0150), arXiv:1210.0150, Theorem 3.8 (for a regular rooted tree over any alphabet of at
least two letters, the group of finite-state automorphisms has a minimal generating set); Kourovka
Archive, Problem 16.86 (Yes, it does), https://arxiv.org/abs/1210.0150.
-/
theorem finiteStateAutomorphismsIrreducibleGenerators_holds :
    finiteStateAutomorphismsIrreducibleGenerators := by
  intro d hd
  let i : Fin d := ⟨0, by omega⟩
  let j : Fin d := ⟨1, by omega⟩
  have hij : i ≠ j := by simp [i, j]
  have : Countable (↥(G d)) := finiteState_countable
  obtain ⟨S, hli, hspan, hcover⟩ := choose_pairs pairClass (many_classes hij)
  obtain ⟨R, hR⟩ := exists_minimal_of_wellFoundedLT
    (fun R : Set (Equiv.Perm (Fin d)) => Subgroup.closure R = ⊤) ⟨Set.univ, Subgroup.closure_univ⟩
  exact ⟨_, generating hij hR.prop hspan hcover, irreducible hij hR hli⟩

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FiniteStateIrreducibleGeneratorsKourovka16Problem86Wanted
